Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: A Galilean telescope (convex objective + concave eyepiece) turns an input ray angle δᵢ into a larger output angle δₒ with magnification exactly f₁/f₂, but only when the lenses are separated by f₁ − f₂ so they share a focal point (the afocal condition).
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): The objective converts input angle into focal-plane offset (d ≈ f₁·δᵢ) and the eyepiece converts that offset back into angle (δₒ ≈ d/f₂), so the angular magnification is exactly f₁/f₂ — provided the two lenses share a focal point.
DEMO STEPS: 4 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

FULL BLUEPRINT:
